\name{cellucid_datasets_list}
\alias{cellucid_datasets_list}
\title{List the datasets to open}
\usage{
cellucid_datasets_list(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{my_datasets} (Most recently opened first), \code{open} (The dataset open now, or null), \code{samples}. Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The datasets this tab can open by name: the built-in samples and the person's own datasets opened before in this browser (My datasets, each with its size and what this browser keeps of it), with the one open now.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{datasets.list} (Datasets). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_datasets_list(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
